Sval: Keep the reading position when the viewport changes width

Gecko adjusts a scroll anchor only after a reflow that starts inside the
anchor's chain. A viewport resize reflows from the root frame, which is in
no chain, so a page narrowed by a Split, a resized window or the Workspace
panel rewraps its text and the reader's place slides down the screen. The
root scroller's anchor is adjusted after a root reflow too, as Chrome
adjusts its anchor after every layout.

diff --git a/layout/base/PresShell.cpp b/layout/base/PresShell.cpp
index 8785ada557..84362ead36 100644
--- a/layout/base/PresShell.cpp
+++ b/layout/base/PresShell.cpp
@@ -10723,6 +10723,13 @@ bool PresShell::DoReflow(nsIFrame* target, bool aInterruptible,
   if (target->IsInScrollAnchorChain()) {
     ScrollAnchorContainer* container = ScrollAnchorContainer::FindFor(target);
     PostPendingScrollAnchorAdjustment(container);
+  } else if (isRoot) {
+    // A reflow from the root, as a viewport resize starts, is never in an
+    // anchor chain, so the root scroller's anchor is adjusted here: text
+    // that rewraps at a new width keeps the reader's place.
+    if (ScrollContainerFrame* rootScroll = GetRootScrollContainerFrame()) {
+      PostPendingScrollAnchorAdjustment(rootScroll->Anchor());
+    }
   }
   if (MOZ_UNLIKELY(isBSizeLimitReflow)) {
     mPresContext->SetVisibleArea(boundsRelativeToTarget);
